The failed tests suggest the purge did not complete when the scheduled job's `execute` was called. The previous version only queued a batch, which does not run until the async queue is flushed (e.g. `Test.stopTest()`), so the test saw nothing deleted. The fix is to purge synchronously in `execute`, in bounded chunks, and hand any remainder to Batch Apex. I have not run this against the test class.

